      "explanation": "Building a prefix\u2011sum array lets each of the 1000 range queries be answered in O(1) instead of iterating over the whole sub\u2011range. This reduces the overall complexity from O(1000\u00b7n) to O(n+1000) and speeds up the kernel for large n while preserving the exact summed result. It assumes n>0 (the driver never calls kernel with n==0) and that 64\u2011bit accumulation is sufficient, both true for the existing workload.",
